 [('negative space','pause / paragraph break','Both can separate groups and make relationships easier to see.'),('margin','room around a thought','A break gives the reader a visible pause before a new group.'),('omission','what remains unsaid','Leaving something out can carry meaning, but essential details must stay.')],
 ['Whitespace need not be white. A paragraph break is a grouping decision, not just decoration.','Omission can create suspense; omitting needed instructions can cause confusion.'],
